00:18:17.116 --> 00:18:24.036
Now, the reason why we do that is that every intermediate
thought is really grounded in real data and never with assumptions.

00:18:25.396 --> 00:18:33.316
So now that we know that the result,
the response is reliable, but how do we actually make sure it's safe?

00:18:33.316 --> 00:18:38.716
So when Jagadeesh received it on his Slack,
there's things that we do, right, which is the final check.

00:18:39.676 --> 00:18:44.036
So the AgentCore policy, which sets the Guardrails is not a one way.

00:18:44.036 --> 00:18:48.756
It's bidirectional. So every answer
also passes through the same Guardrails,

00:18:48.756 --> 00:18:54.396
ensuring that PII data or secrets or denied
topics that Jagadeesh cannot see.

00:18:55.076 --> 00:19:05.036
So these things are stripped. So what reaches Slack is being cleared,
not just generated by the model, only the data that is allowed.

00:19:05.596 --> 00:19:08.196
That the user is allowed to see passes through.

00:19:09.156 --> 00:19:12.996
